<article class="env-corollary" id="15528F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/15528F">Corollary <span data-tag="15528F">5.5.5.8</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a presentable $\infty $-category, let $S$ be a saturated collection of morphisms of $\calC $, and suppose that $S$ is of small generation. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &amp;  Y \ar [dr]^{g} &amp;  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^{h} &amp;  &amp;  Z}  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram in $\calC $. If $f$ and $h$ belong to $S$, then $g$ belongs to $S$. </p>
</article>
